                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "mispunches"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "044dcd41-45e7-33fe-a120-b904c57e17b9",
                        "entry_id": "ea47647b-35c5-3ec6-b2aa-1ea1259f464d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An act or result of mispunching (any sense)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f5fc5f47-2bf3-41a6-b61c-f0c5b70fba4d",
                                "sense_id": "044dcd41-45e7-33fe-a120-b904c57e17b9",
                                "text": "What happens when a mispunch is found in an input record?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "98c7b62d-b125-41e2-8488-5dfecd726695",
                                "sense_id": "044dcd41-45e7-33fe-a120-b904c57e17b9",
                                "text": "Therefore, a two-handed punch gives a greater contact area than a one-handed, and reduces the chances of a mispunch ( see illustration 216 )."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "069bbcf8-0b5f-41c1-80b0-e997e5f326f3",
                                "sense_id": "044dcd41-45e7-33fe-a120-b904c57e17b9",
                                "text": "Upon removal of the mispunch and reanalysis, two other points in this data set emerge as possible outliers."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0551fd5b-c8bb-43b6-8e08-75b469255f3c",
                                "sense_id": "044dcd41-45e7-33fe-a120-b904c57e17b9",
                                "text": "The interior ring on the disk occurs very occasionally on Howland's types 52B, C, and E. (Agora IV, pp. 181–185, 186–188); in this case it may simply be the result of a mispunch of the central filling-hole."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4c676408-8014-47a6-8559-cf44c751a7fe",
                                "sense_id": "044dcd41-45e7-33fe-a120-b904c57e17b9",
                                "text": "If you have an 'mp', or mispunch, it means you went to a wrong control, or missed one out, and are, unfortunately, disqualified."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
            {
                "entry_id": "35d69657-6c1c-3a7c-b433-b7e868d86032",
